# Goldens that emit but do not type-check as Swift yet: the Swift backend's work queue, each with
# the reason. scripts/typecheck-swift.sh skips them; a case leaves this list when it type-checks.
#
# Flow narrowing: Bloom narrows an optional after `if x != none`, `x || y`, a ternary; Swift needs
# `if let` or `!`. Needs the checker's name resolution (bloom_lang::backend NameRes), not spans.
state_narrowing    # narrowing after `!= none`
narrow_paren       # narrowing through parentheses
ternary_none       # narrowing in a ternary
optional_or        # an optional as a truth value
# TypeScript-shaped data with no Swift meaning yet (structural records, `Partial`, JS `Map`).
records            # structural records, `Partial<T>`
record_types       # a record type alias
record_key_index   # a record indexed by key
record_spread_override  # a record spread with an override
keyed_match        # `Partial<T>`
collections        # JS `Map<K, V>`
# BloomUI nodes and screen chrome not on SwiftUI yet.
inline_view        # ErrorBoundary
mixed_runs         # RawText
optional_binding   # MenuContent
screen_named       # Screen (the screen node and its chrome)
# Emitter gaps.
equality           # a recursive (indirect) enum's structural `==`
equal_member       # a public view whose props are internal: its `body` must still be public
soft_names         # a view member named like `body`
view_alias         # a type alias of a view
list_methods       # a statement printed on one line with the next
virtual_list_row   # `VirtualList` over `enumerated()`
union_casts        # the stdlib's number formatting labels (`fractionDigits:`)
